    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0230" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>

                <head>No. 115.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Osborn.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 87.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 132, in which you inclose a copy of a note from the Chilian Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs, soliciting the friendly offices of the legations of the United
                    States at La Paz and Santiago, in securing an exchange of prisoners of war
                    between Chili and Bolivia, and to say in reply that Mr. Adams, who succeeds Mr.
                    Pettis in the mission to Bolivia, presently departs for his post at La Paz and
                    will be instructed in the direction desired. The person in charge of the
                    archives of the legation at La Paz is not authorized to act in a diplomatic
                    sense.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
